From 3fa92d3f98c65bbb14c286eaf3492c885b8e0080 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix persistent map-disappearing bug, add ErrorBoundary,
 tap-to-place, plan import, code-splitting, haversine distance

- Add top-level React ErrorBoundary (previously none existed, so ANY
  uncaught render/effect exception silently blanked the entire app -
  the most likely cause of the map-disappearing bug surviving two
  prior fix attempts, since those only guarded individual Leaflet
  calls, not the app as a whole).
- Guard the one remaining unguarded Leaflet call (createMarkerIcon)
  and validate marker coordinates before rendering.
- Dedupe/validate draft points before they reach Leaflet's
  polygon/polyline renderer to avoid degenerate geometry.
- Fix missing min-h-0 on the map's flex container (classic flexbox
  collapse bug).
- Force map.invalidateSize() when any modal opens/closes, since
  Radix Dialog/Sheet body-scroll-lock layout shifts aren't always
  caught by a container-only ResizeObserver.
- Add tap-to-place mobile fallback (HTML5 drag-and-drop never fires
  on touch devices): tap a resource card to arm it, tap the map to
  place, stays armed for placing multiples.
- Add Import Plan (JSON) next to Export, with runtime validation.
- Seed INITIAL_MARKERS on first visit instead of a blank map.
- Lazy-load MapContainer/Leaflet + manual Vite chunks for
  Leaflet/Radix, eliminating the >500KB single-bundle build warning.
- Replace naive Math.hypot lat/lng distance with proper haversine
  for nearest-municipality lookup.
- Fix 3 pre-existing lint errors (empty interfaces, require() import).
- Remove orphaned/unused src/utils/geo.ts left over from a prior
  incomplete session.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint 0 errors, vite build succeeds
with split chunks (leaflet 149KB, radix 113KB, main 372KB vs prior
single 631KB bundle).
